    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math education by adapting explanations to a student's level and style, offering instant feedback, and turning abstract concepts into stories or visuals. They can tutor 24/7, reduce fear of asking 'stupid' questions, and make math feel more human and less intimidating, especially for diverse learners."
